arding software lifecycle and cybersecurity.", "support_note": "Directly states the requirement for a robust software development lifecycle.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.75, "evidence_links": [{"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Highlights the requirement for repeatability, reliability and performance in devices with software."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-c-design-development", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Establishes design control requirements for devices automated with computer software."}, {"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Emphasizes the need for a robust software development lifecycle, including risk management and cybersecurity."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Provides device confidence score data related to the missed event. Further analysis of this log may reveal contributing factors."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Provides device confidence score data related to the missed event. Further analysis of this log may reveal contributing factors."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "A minor, non-recurrent ventricular tachycardia-adjacent irregularity was detected by the remote monitoring center, but a clinician note documenting it was not filed. While no adverse patient outcome occurred and the event is being handled at a monitoring/investigation level, the lack of a documented record raises concerns about potential recurrence or missed detection in the future. This requires investigation to determine why the clinician note was missing and whether any systemic issues contributed to this gap in documentation. The device incorporates software (EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1) and is automated with computer software (21 CFR \